name>Abou Atme</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gynecological tumors revealing hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer: analysis of a large Lebanese pedigree</article-title><source>Int J Gyn Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>16</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1516</fpage><lpage>1521</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1525-1438.2006.00621.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Risinger</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrett</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lynch</surname><given-names>HT</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyd</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular genetic evidence of the occurrence of breast cancer as an integral tumor in patients with the hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal carcinoma syndrome</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1996</year><volume>77</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1836</fpage><lpage>1843</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8646682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1097-0142(19960501)77:9&#x0003c;1836::AID-CNCR12&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Westenend</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sch&#x000fc;tte</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoogmans</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dinjens</surname><given-names>WN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Breast cancer in an MSH2 gene mutation carrier</article-title><source>Hum Pathol</source><year>2005</year><volume>36</volume><issue>12</issue><fpage>1322</fpage><lpage>1326</lpage><pub-id pub-id-ty